# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even on Windows checkouts.
#
# They run inside Linux containers, where /bin/sh is dash. A CRLF file makes dash read
# line 1 as `set -u<CR>` and abort with "set: Illegal option -" before a single test runs.
# Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, which rewrites text files to CRLF on
# checkout — so without this, the integration harness is broken on any Windows clone.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by Linux tooling inside the images.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
